WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.160
The SCP Foundation depends on staying out of&nbsp;
the public eye, and away from public perception,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:11.440
in order to accomplish their vital work. If the&nbsp;
public were to find out about the Foundation and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:17.280
the nightmares it spends every day protecting us&nbsp;
from, it would be total chaos, worldwide. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:22.720
would be so busy trying to field attention&nbsp;
from civilians, politicians, and reporters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:28.880
fending off every random Joe with a smartphone who&nbsp;
wanted to take an Instagram story of SCP-096 and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:34.720
endanger his life, that they wouldn’t have time to&nbsp;
contain all the world-ending anomalies out there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:40.720
So, they operate entirely under the radar.
But it wasn’t always this way. There was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:46.160
a time when the world at large knew about the&nbsp;
SCP Foundation, and the researchers had to find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:52.160
out a way to step out of the spotlight for good.&nbsp;
Like everything else about the SCP Foundation, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:57.840
wasn’t easy. The road to the Foundation’s current&nbsp;
cloak of secrecy was paved with trial and error,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:04.400
experimental magic, and a formidable woman&nbsp;
known by the alias Elizabeth Crocker. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:11.600
is the story of SCP-001 “The Frontispiece,”&nbsp;
also known as the Pickman-Blank proposal.&nbsp;

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:17.120
It all started in 1964, when several national&nbsp;
governments discovered that the Foundation’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:22.480
Overwatch Command was working both for and against&nbsp;
all of the countries involved in the Cold War.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:29.360
Canada, the USSR, Israel and Lebanon, and&nbsp;
Egypt all withdrew support for the Foundation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.440
The most catastrophic was the withdrawal of&nbsp;
support from the United States government,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:38.720
ordered by Lyndon B. Johnson after his national&nbsp;
security team discovered the Foundation had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:43.920
been involved in the Cuban Missile Crisis.
At the same time as the Foundation’s relationship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:49.280
with these global powers was crumbling, the&nbsp;
Foundation made one of its most powerful enemies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:55.840
ever. Person of Interest 001, also known by&nbsp;
her alias “Elizabeth Crocker” was a member&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:02.240
of the CIA beginning in 1959. There, she fell&nbsp;
in love with a fellow agent named Dr. Alexandre&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:06.960
Hilbert, who was working on a Quantum&nbsp;
Brace capable of altering probability.&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:12.000
In 1964, the Foundation reached out to&nbsp;
Dr. Hilbert in an attempt to recruit him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.640
but he refused. Shortly after this, he was&nbsp;
killed during a test of the Quantum Brace.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:22.000
Crocker attributed his death to the Foundation,&nbsp;
believing them to have tampered with his machine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:27.120
in order to punish him for turning down their&nbsp;
offer. After the death of her love, Crocker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:34.960
swore to destroy the SCP Foundation for good.
On October 19, 1967, Crocker disguised herself as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:40.560
the personal driver of a member of the O5 Council&nbsp;
and shot her one dozen times before dropping her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:46.320
body outside of a Foundation safe house in&nbsp;
San Francisco. A note was found on the body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:52.320
with a message from Elizabeth Crocker. It ended&nbsp;
with this promise: “It’s high time somebody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:58.880
broke up your tidy little racket. No, more&nbsp;
than one somebody. Everybody. We’re going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:04.720
contain you, and you’re going to suffocate.”
Agent Crocker endangered the Foundation’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:09.600
security, seeming to possess a knowledge of&nbsp;
all of its outposts as well as the ability to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:14.640
decipher even its most secure communications&nbsp;
ciphers. Several members of personnel holed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:20.240
up in Havana, Cuba during January of 1968&nbsp;
began to brainstorm, looking for a way to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:25.120
increase security and keep the Foundation&nbsp;
together in the face of these new threats.&nbsp;

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:29.680
A number of different researchers were&nbsp;
in attendance, including Dr. Arik Euler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:35.280
a Thaumatologist, or a scientist in the field of&nbsp;
ritual magic. Though some of his colleagues failed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:40.560
to treat him with the respect he deserved, some&nbsp;
out of skepticism and some out of outright bigotry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:46.960
toward his Jewish identity, Euler was a brilliant&nbsp;
mind with an idea that could save them all.&nbsp;

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:52.320
Dr. Euler proposed a potential solution to the&nbsp;
chaos spreading across the world, as companies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:57.520
owned by the Foundation were being exposed and&nbsp;
destroyed and their facilities reduced to rubble.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:02.720
Dr. Euler suggested that it might be possible to&nbsp;
place some sort of illusion over the businesses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:08.160
acting as fronts for the Foundation, preventing&nbsp;
them from being found out by any outsiders.&nbsp;

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:13.200
Kady O’Donnel responded that that wouldn’t be&nbsp;
enough, that they needed to find a way to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:20.080
the world to forget the Foundation existed at all,&nbsp;
at least for a little while. Dr. Euler, at a loss,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:24.880
reached out to Site-43 to see if they had&nbsp;
any thaumatologists at their facility.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:31.360
There was one, in fact, Dr. Okorie. Dr. Edwin&nbsp;
Falkirk and Chief of Security and Containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:36.400
Martin Strauss were sent in to brief him on the&nbsp;
situation at hand. During their conversation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:41.120
Okorie reported thaumaturgic changes made&nbsp;
around his place of work. The information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:46.800
he shared caught Strauss’ attention immediately.
After a moment of thought, Strauss knew exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:52.000
what it meant and who was behind it. It was&nbsp;
a sign from someone who would prove immensely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:59.200
helpful, and a mysterious man named Thilo Zwist.
Thilo Zwist, also known as Person of Interest-382&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:05.120
as well as a long list of aliases, is a highly&nbsp;
skilled cryptomancer, who has used his control of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:10.800
anomalies to render himself functionally immortal.&nbsp;
He performs a form of magic using language,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:16.080
and was previously associated with an organization&nbsp;
known as the giftschreiber, or the “Poison&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:21.680
Writers.” Since his discovery, Zwist has spent&nbsp;
decades involved in a cat and mouse game of sorts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:28.720
with Site-43 Director Dr. V.L. Scout. Now, the&nbsp;
same Dr. Scout had planted a reference to Zwist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:34.400
in the mind of Dr. Okorie, to suggest that the&nbsp;
Foundation contact the elusive man for help.&nbsp;

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:41.040
With this new plan in motion, Dr. Okorie attempted&nbsp;
to make contact with Zwist in March of 1968.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:45.520
He met the man at an abandoned building&nbsp;
in the Harbourfront district of Toronto.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:50.160
There, he found Zwist, who claimed to be&nbsp;
expecting him. He teased Okorie about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:55.680
unwanted attention the Foundation was receiving,&nbsp;
as well as the danger posed by Elizabeth Crocker.&nbsp;

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:01.520
Eventually, he asked, “Are you here to ask&nbsp;
for my help, or did I let you find me for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:07.200
no good reason?” Okorie admitted that he was&nbsp;
seeking help, and Zwist explained his special&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:13.120
method of combining writing with ritual magic in&nbsp;
order to imbue the words with power or danger.&nbsp;

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:19.040
He offered to craft a phrase, a series of words&nbsp;
that, when written on a sign created by him, would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:25.200
keep the public from seeing who the foundation&nbsp;
truly was. He offered to do it exactly once, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:32.000
not recreate it going forward. All he needed was&nbsp;
a piece of language to craft his spell. Dr. Okorie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:38.640
offered an initialism as a possibility, suggesting&nbsp;
the “SCP” that comes before the Foundation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:45.760
Zwist laughed delightedly at this, and said&nbsp;
simply, “This is going to work out splendidly.”&nbsp;

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:52.000
One week later, Zwist brought Dr. Okorie a simple&nbsp;
logo design for a nonexistent business, called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:56.880
“Scout’s Cargo Packing,” as well as a chemical&nbsp;
formula for an antidote that would inoculate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:02.400
anyone who received it against the sign’s magical&nbsp;
properties. After approval by the O5 Council,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:07.200
the logo was printed on a fleet of moving trucks&nbsp;
that could then be used to transport personnel and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:12.960
items across North America without any detection.&nbsp;
It was highly effective, and the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:18.000
began plans to spread this new protective&nbsp;
measure throughout all of its facilities.&nbsp;

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:24.480
In May of 1968, a collision along Route 66 in&nbsp;
the United States damaged one of the trucks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:30.240
removing its magical functionality. Curious about&nbsp;
the repercussions of Zwist’s work being destroyed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:35.120
and about any potentially dangerous&nbsp;
effects, Dr. Euler formed the Mimesis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:41.280
and Cryptomancy Research Group, where he worked&nbsp;
alongside Dr. Okorie, and Dr. Ilse Reynders.&nbsp;

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:45.760
As Dr. Reynders suffered from a condition that&nbsp;
rendered her unable to leave a sealed chamber&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:52.560
in Site-43, Euler was reassigned to that facility&nbsp;
and worked alongside her and Okorie there. During&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:57.280
their research, the team learned that damage&nbsp;
to Zwist’s writing changed its properties in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:02.960
a variety of ways, and he continued breaking&nbsp;
down the trucks to try and understand them.&nbsp;

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:08.560
Meanwhile, Elizabeth Crocker had not let up in her&nbsp;
dogged pursuit of the Foundation’s destruction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:12.880
A shipping container bearing the insignia&nbsp;
of a defunct Foundation front company was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:19.360
discovered in the port of Los Angeles on July&nbsp;
2, 1968, containing the badly beaten - but still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:26.400
alive - Abrasha Sokolsky. A note was pinned to&nbsp;
his tie, reading: “Can you feel the noose yet?”&nbsp;

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:32.320
Back at Site-43, Euler, Reynders, and Okorie&nbsp;
reached a breakthrough. The power of Zwist’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:39.440
work came, not from the full words of “Scout’s&nbsp;
Cargo Packing,” but from the initials SCP itself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:44.000
Using a combination of grammar and magic,&nbsp;
much to the excitement of every English&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:49.840
teacher and fantasy fan, they could transfer&nbsp;
the properties of Zwist’s sign to any other sign&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:56.560
bearing the same initials. Just like it always&nbsp;
has at the Foundation, it all came down to S. C.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:00.720
P. A variety of former front&nbsp;
businesses were revived,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:06.800
all bearing the same initials. There was Star&nbsp;
City Poker, Supply, Control, and Purification,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:11.520
and of course, Sawyer’s Cheesy Pretzels.
The high from this breakthrough quickly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:17.040
gave way to another devastating loss, however,&nbsp;
as Agent Crocker struck again. In Johannesburg,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:23.520
South Africa, Agent Crocker infiltrated an SCP&nbsp;
Site under the alias “Dr. Gabrielle Fish.” There,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:29.120
she exacerbated existing racial tensions and took&nbsp;
advantage of the Apartheid state to sow discord.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:33.520
Crocker killed Regional Director Jansen&nbsp;
and dumped his body near Site 19,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:38.240
with a note in his jacket pocket. It&nbsp;
said: “You’re running out of continents.”&nbsp;

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:43.200
As the research team kicked their efforts into&nbsp;
high gear, preparing an official research proposal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:48.400
on Quantum Linguaphysics, Elizabeth Crocker&nbsp;
continued her grim work. In the People’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:54.400
Republic of China, she used cryptomancy to trigger&nbsp;
severe paranoia in Chairman Mao Zedong, drawing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:58.800
his attention to Foundation representatives&nbsp;
hiding in the People’s Republic of China.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:04.320
This forced Dr. Noble to escape the country,&nbsp;
leaving behind any Foundation influence in China.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:10.640
There was, yet again, a note left for her. “Five&nbsp;
minutes to midnight.” Crocker was closing in.&nbsp;

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:15.920
Next, Crocker aligned herself with US President&nbsp;
Richard Nixon, tipping him off to the existence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:21.600
of the Foundation and convincing him to have&nbsp;
the US Army occupy the facility. Euler, Okorie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:27.760
and Reynders had to act, and act fast. Each of&nbsp;
the Doctors tentatively signed off on the project,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:32.240
ready to put the experiment into practice.
Meanwhile, Crocker got bolder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:36.400
and more violent. She killed Foundation&nbsp;
personnel whenever she got the chance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:41.760
abandoning long-form political strategy in&nbsp;
favor of spectacle. She used an auditory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:47.280
cryptomantic agent, embedded in a recording&nbsp;
of “I Wanna Hold Your Hand” by The Beatles,&nbsp;

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:51.520
to kill ten Foundation personnel&nbsp;
in a safe house in Scotland. Next,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:56.800
she infiltrated Site-43, where she was&nbsp;
defeated by intervention from Zwist himself.&nbsp;

00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:05.520
At Site-01, on July 9, 1969, Dr. Euler and&nbsp;
Dr. Okorie now put their creation into place,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:11.360
called the Frontispiece. Within two weeks, its&nbsp;
effects had spread across the world, cloaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:17.360
every Foundation front in its anomalous effects.&nbsp;
By June of 1970, the Foundation could come out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:22.880
of frightened, panicked hiding, and resume&nbsp;
regular hiding. They were working actively in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:29.760
the world again, building new sites all the time.
In August of 1971, one of the Foundation’s trucks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:34.080
was unable to cross beyond the Berlin wall,&nbsp;
as the guards stationed there only read the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:40.320
Cyrillic alphabet. Dr. Euler proposed a solution,&nbsp;
in the form of a New York-based artist whose work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:46.080
possessed similar properties to Zwist’s writing.&nbsp;
This artist was a man named Andy Warhol,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:50.320
and the Foundation commissioned him to create&nbsp;
an imagery-based version of the Frontispiece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:54.560
compatible with all known languages,&nbsp;
allowing the effects to extend to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.560 --> 00:12:00.160
regions that used different alphabets.
In the later 1970s, Crocker resurfaced and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:06.160
escaped custody, and shortly after Dr. Okorie&nbsp;
was found murdered in his home. She remained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:11.760
active through the 80s, aligning herself with the&nbsp;
Reagan administration in an ineffective attempt to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:16.480
make him launch an attack on the Foundation.&nbsp;
Currently, it is believed that she is dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:22.400
as she would now be over one hundred years&nbsp;
old. However, if Zwist is any indication,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:27.360
there are tools out there that might have allowed&nbsp;
her to extend her life far beyond what is natural.&nbsp;

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:30.960
To this day, the work of the&nbsp;
original research team lives on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:37.280
even as the scientists behind it have passed&nbsp;
away. It is highly effective, with one exception:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:41.680
repeated exposure to anomalous activity&nbsp;
renders someone immune to the effects of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:47.440
Frontispiece. Otherwise, however, the Foundation&nbsp;
remains secured, contained, and protected.&nbsp;

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:53.440
A final letter from Thilo Zwist was discovered&nbsp;
among Dr. Euler’s effects after his death in 2013,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:57.440
reminding them of their duty to protect&nbsp;
the world and do the right thing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.440 --> 00:13:03.360
He ended the letter with this: “your course was&nbsp;
set the moment I baked that lovely little flaw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:09.520
into the Writing which you stole. I robbed you&nbsp;
of the opportunity to become the tyrants of all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:15.920
our nightmares. You will have no choice but to be&nbsp;
better than that, because evil only flourishes in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:22.960
ease. You will never know ease. You, and those who&nbsp;
come after you, will need to keep doing the work.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:29.840
You will get to decide how well you do it, of&nbsp;
course. And on that matter, I have a suggestion:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:37.520
Do it right. Stop Compromising Principles.”
Now go check out “SCP-001 - When Day Breaks”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:44.640
and “SCP-001 - The Scarlet King” for more&nbsp;
insights into the fascinating world of SCP-001!

